{
  "$comment": "DDD bridge for IBM Carbon v11. Tiers follow elements/d-d-d/design-system/bridge/contract.json. Named DDD colors point at fixed Carbon palette values (@carbon/colors DTCG) by role; theme chrome uses Carbon's white (light) and g100 (dark) theme tokens. Font stacks and weights are copied from @carbon/type (it ships them as JS, not tokens). Kept as DDD on purpose: font weights medium and black (Carbon has light, regular and semibold only), state opacities (Carbon uses hover colors, not opacity), border widths (same 1-4px values), and heading/body sizes (Carbon body-01 is 14px, below the 16px floor; body size is an open decision for every bridge). Carbon's spacing scale (2, 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 40, 48px...) sits on DDD's 4px grid, so the theme chrome uses DDD spacing tokens with the same values; @carbon/styles only exposes its spacing variables inside component scopes.",
